# patches/groups - named sets of profiles a patch's header can name (issue 189)
#
# For a general audience: a patch's header says which profiles take it.
# When several profiles take the same set of patches, the set gets a name
# here, and those patches say the name; adding a profile to the set is then
# one line, here, instead of one in every patch's header. Read by
# scripts/plan-patches, which the patch runner asks for each profile's
# patches (issue 189c), so a name here reaches the build at once.
#
# One group a line: "name: profile profile ...". Lines starting with "#"
# and blank lines are ignored.

# the buddy patches: the buddy module, its clan and roster tables, its maps
# and stand-ins (issue 617), taken by basic and by the custom client's test
# server; the econ profile (issue 192) joins it when it is registered
buddy-set: basic cc-test
